{"event": "report", "t": 1795262230.755, "claim": "fixed", "text": "rformance` already excludes `CANCELLED`.\n2. **Catalog-only products produced NULL-month rows.** The model started from products and used left joins, so every product with no sales added a row with `sales_month = NULL`. There were 4 such rows.\n\n**The change** (`/app/dbt_models_duckdb/models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql`)\n- The joins now start from order lines and use inner joins, so only real sales rows are produced.\n- The filter excludes `CANCELLED` orders and any order flagged `EXCLUDE_FROM_REPORTING`, `TEST_ORDER_FLAG`, `SAMPLE_ORDER_FLAG`, or `INTERNAL_ORDER_FLAG`. Nulls count as not flagged.\n- Output columns, aliases, `group by`, and materialization are unchanged. Upstream staging models are untouched.\n\n**Results**\n\n| | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rows | 202 | 192 |\n| NULL-month rows | 4 | 0 |\n| Revenue | 722,313.24 | 625,348.70 |\n| Units sold | 6,590 | 5,740 |\n| Gross profit | 608,293.75 | 526,846.83 |\n\nThe after figures match an independent query on the staging tables.\n\n**Verification:** `dbt run --select rpt_category_performance` succeeds. This model has no tests of its own, and I did not run the project's 814 tests. The Snowflake project is unchanged, since `DB_TYPE=duckdb`.\n\n**Choices and open questions for you**\n- **Category column:** it is still `product_type`, which holds only PHYSICAL, DIGITAL, SERVICE, and GIFT_CARD. That looks like a misnamed column rather than a category. The real category data has a `primary_category_id` that links cleanly, but the category mapping's `is_primary` flag disagrees with it for 438 products. I didn't switch sources on a guess, so this needs a decision from you.\n- **RETURNED orders** still count toward revenue and units. Some reports exclude them, so confirm the business definition.\n- **Test/sample/internal exclusions** go beyond the cancelled filter. Drop them if your team counts those orders as sales.\n- **`avg_unit_price`** is an unweighted average of line unit prices. I left it as is.\n\nVERDICT: fixed", "verdict": null}
